# CODEOWNERS for the Plone Conference Organizers Handbook.
#
# STATUS: a proposal (decision D8), not a decision.
# Nothing in this file binds anyone until the community accepts the stewardship
# model described in docs/running/governance.md.
#
# INTENDED MODEL, after community buy-in:
#   - At least three maintainers across at least two organizations are named here.
#   - Each chapter names a steward and a deputy in its front matter, and the
#     steward and the deputy come from different organizations.
#   - Paths are mapped to GitHub teams, for example:
#       /docs/workstreams/marketing/   @plone/conference-marketing
#   - The Plone Foundation holds repository admin after the transfer to the
#     plone organization.
#   - A bus-factor figure (distinct people who can merge) is reported at each
#     annual release.
# The three-maintainer gate does not apply to version 1.
#
# INTERIM ENTRY, while the repository incubates under the syslabcom organization:
# the incubation team is the only owner of every path. Replace the handle with
# a dedicated handbook team when one exists. The team must have write access
# to this repository, otherwise GitHub ignores the rule.

* @syslabcom/syslab-com
